+      "contracts": "Forcing allow_exhaustion_state_ref=True in _emit_repeat_until_from_emitter_input brings back at 2.29+ a shortcut the design deliberately removed: any match case whose variant equals the exhaustion variant reads loop state, so a done with that variant but different data returns state instead of its payload. This changes the lowering of every union loop result at 2.29+, not only results with path fields.",
+      "generality": "Nested and multiple inactive path fields work. A path field inside the exhausted variant taken from state still emits a relpath ref in _loop_on_exhausted_outputs and is still rejected at 2.29+, although 2.28 compiles it.",
+      "fit": "Fixing this in the compiler and falling back to the frame's continue projection, as 2.28 does, is reasonable. However, the patch undoes a deliberate target gate instead of fixing reference resolution."
