+      "contracts": "The new dereference in _resolve_structured_output_artifacts runs at every target and on every loop-output value shaped like {ref: str}, not only on exhaustion overrides. A legitimate map or json value of that shape is therefore now treated as a reference.",
+      "generality": "All override ref kinds (placeholders, state refs, path fields inside the exhausted variant) are followed at the only place generated code consumes loop outputs, and they give 2.28's snapshot values.",
+      "fit": "Ref chasing is added to one consumer instead of at the exhaustion producer or the shared bound-address resolver. It also brings legacy {ref} payload handling into the typed runtime path, which _resolve_runtime_value explicitly refuses."
