+      "contracts": "As in R302, the dereference in executor.py _resolve_structured_output_artifacts runs at every target on any loop-output value shaped like {ref}, and this version does not even check that the ref is a string.",
+      "generality": "Nested and multiple inactive path fields work, but a path field inside the exhausted variant taken from state is still rejected at 2.29+, although 2.28 compiles it.",
+      "fit": "Bringing the compiler in line with the validator is sound, but ref chasing is again added to a single typed consumer rather than at the producer or the resolver."
+    },
+    "summary": "Drops relpath fields from the exhaustion placeholders and makes structured-output resolution follow {ref} values read from loop outputs."
