+      "generality": "It covers every bound consumer and every generated ref kind (the patch also exercises called and branched loops). It drops the caller's scope when following the ref, which is harmless only because generated refs are currently root-level.",
+      "fit": "The layer concern is the same as R406: legacy ref-payload chasing is added to the typed bound resolver, and persisted frames keep raw refs."
+    },
+    "summary": "Moves the relpath rejection after the generated-ref allowance and makes every bound loop-output read follow stored {ref} values."
+  },
+  "R863": {
